These non-islander communities total an estimated 110,820 residents. A smaller immigrant stream comes from [[Sarta]], [[Volisania]], [[Balboa]], [[Balisca]], and other mainland or overseas communities.

By the 2010s and 2020s, the main migration pressures were different. Guajicutea became attractive to retirees from [[Sarta]], and foreign home buying pushed up urban property prices. The government later responded with restrictions on foreign purchases in the most expensive areas and with easier entry rules for foreign workers through golden visa-style reforms and the 2017 digital nomad visa.

